NimbyHands (display name Hands) is a fork of Give&Take.

Original work: Give&Take, Steam Workshop item 2903112334
  https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2903112334
Author: affenb3rt (contact listed on the Workshop page as Discord)
Credited contributor (from the mod's config): Wardog
Original build: PBO version 23040119, packed with Mikero DePbo 8.07; Workshop last updated April 1, 2023.
Imported: October 14, 2026, from the copy recorded in
  logs/Copy-WorkshopItem-2903112334-20261014-153144.log
  (GiveAndTake.pbo sha256 EDBC6A285C15511CCF53FFFE2E3A3EF98C09759C00707B202496FF264C671574)

Permission: the original ships no license file. The Workshop description, read October 14, 2026,
grants permission to repack, reupload, modify, and redistribute the mod. The dated capture of that
text is PERMISSION.md in this folder; if the author changes the terms, re-check before the next
release.

Import notes:
- Scripts, inputs.xml, and languagecore/stringtable.csv are byte-for-byte copies.
- config.cpp is the original config.bin decoded to text; values are unchanged.
- logo.paa and Texheaders.bin were not imported; the NIMBY pack supplies its own mod presentation.

Players: the input actions were renamed on October 19, 2026. Anyone who changed the offer/request
key from O, or bound the pocket toggle, binds it once more under Options > Controls > NIMBY
("Hands: offer or request item", "Hands: open or close pockets").

Changes made for the NIMBY | HARDCORE | BADLANDS | 1pp server are listed below, newest first.
- October 20, 2026 (test finding NIMBY-T-007): Data/Inputs.xml declares the sorting group "nimby"
  (label NIMBY) inside <inputs>, where 1.30 reads it; both Hands bindings now appear under a NIMBY tab
  in Options > Controls instead of Unsorted. No input names or defaults changed.
- October 19, 2026 (Hands plan Phase 2, decisions G1 and G2): renamed the addon from NimbyGiveTake
  to NimbyHands - folder, PBO, CfgPatches and CfgMods classes, every custom class and member
  (NimbyHands*), input actions (UANimbyOfferRequestItem to UANimbyHandsOfferRequest,
  UANimbyTogglePocketAccess to UANimbyHandsTogglePockets), string keys (STR_NIMBY_GT_* to
  STR_NIMBY_HANDS_*), log prefix ([NIMBY][GiveTake] to [NIMBY][Hands]), and profile folder
  ($profile:NimbyHands). inputs.xml moved to Data/Inputs.xml (sorted into the vanilla Others
  controls tab at the time, which 1.30 did not honor; see October 20): offer/request stays on O;
  the pocket toggle ships unbound with the label "Hands: open or close pockets" (the Left Shift + O combo also fired offer/request, test finding NIMBY-T-002).
  The two input labels are plain text now, so their string keys were removed. The pocket
  notification names the toggle's binding. Added PERMISSION.md for the Workshop permission text.
- October 19, 2026 (Hands plan Phase 1):
  - Every transfer is registered in a server-side in-flight registry with a correlation id before
    it is dispatched; a second request for an item already in flight is refused. Nothing is
    persisted.
  - Consent, both players' state (alive, conscious, not restrained, not in a vehicle, not
    swimming, still connected, not replaced), distance, the source item, the destination, and the
    engine's own move test are checked again immediately before dispatch.
  - The fixed one-second outcome check was replaced by lifecycle lines REQUESTED, CONFIRMED,
    REFUSED, and UNCONFIRMED, one terminal line per request: CONFIRMED comes from the item's
    location-change event on the server; a bounded 5-second timeout reconciles where the item is
    and never retries, clones, restores, or deletes anything.
  - Pockets (G4): the toggle cannot be used while restrained; the server closes open pockets on
    unconsciousness, restraint, reconnect, and respawn; Put In Pockets refuses an unconscious or
    restrained player. The toggle and every forced close write a pockets line.
  - Log lines carry both player ids (BI id and Steam64); names are quoted and escaped; debug
    lines appear only when $profile:<addon>\debug exists. A self-test runs when
    $profile:<addon>\selftest exists.
  - Removed the #ifdef DIAG blocks in the give and take actions, which set a state and never
    cleared it.
- October 14, 2026 (review CR-001): rewrote the transfer routine (NimbyMoveItemToPlayer). It now
  asks the player holding the item to move it with the vanilla server path (ServerTakeToDst), which
  runs through that player's own hand state machine, instead of deleting the item's network state
  and injecting fake hand events on both players. Transfers land in the receiver's inventory
  (cargo or an attachment slot), never their hands; Give now delivers to inventory and the
  "take to hands" action was removed. Each transfer logs REQUESTED, then OK or FAILED once the
  receiver has checked where the item ended up.
- October 14, 2026 (review CR-005, CR-006, CR-003):
  - Renamed every class, input action, string key, and member with a Nimby prefix so the fork
    cannot collide with the original or another mod; fixed misspellings (Pocktes, Toggel, Cancle)
    and renamed the two misspelled script files. The modded GameConstants member became
    NimbyGiveTakeConstants. Addon, CfgMods class, and PBO prefix are now NimbyGiveTake.
  - Every transfer now writes one [NIMBY][GiveTake] line to the server script log naming the
    action, result, giver, receiver, and item. Expected refusals (no item, no space, item already
    taken) are logged there instead of raising Error() with no context.
  - The pocket-access toggle, unbound in the original, defaults to Left Shift + O.
- October 14, 2026: removed the four CfgMods picture and logo entries that point at logo.paa,
  which is not imported. Without this, the game logs a missing-file error for the image.
